    "id": 562457610,
    "iid": 566,
    "project_id": 6329679,
    "title": "feat: allow hpa.minReplicas to be set to 0",
    "description": "<!--\nThis is a general Merge Request template.\nConsider choosing a template from the list above if it will match your case more.\n-->\n\n## What does this MR do?\n\nChart need update to support new kubernetes 1.37 changes.\n\n## Why was this MR needed?\n\nKubernetes 1.37 now allows minReplicas to be set to 0 (see: https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release/#beta-horizontalpodautoscaler-scale-to-zero) and is on by default\nSo minReplicas: 0 is now a reasonable thing to ask for, and the chart silently overrides it.\n\nThe template now uses hasKey, so an explicit 0 is kept and the default stays 1 when the key is unset. I added a note in values.yaml: scaling to zero only works with at least one Object or External metric (the API server rejects Pods and Resource metrics with minReplicas: 0). I also added tests/hpa_test.yaml.\n\n## What's the best way to test this MR?\n\nTested with helm unittest (92/92 passing) and helm template for minReplicas unset, 0 and 3.\n\n## What are the relevant issue numbers?\n\nNone",
