  {
    "id": 549882741,
    "iid": 562,
    "project_id": 6329679,
    "title": "fix: reject unknown keys and non-map entries in rbac.rules",
    "description": "## What does this MR do?\n\nThe chart renders only `apiGroups`, `resources` and `verbs` from each `rbac.rules` entry. A misspelled key, such as `resource_names`, was dropped without a message, so the Role was wider than the user wrote. A `null` or string entry failed with a raw template error.\n\nThis MR fails the render for these cases. The error names the rule index and the unsupported keys. It follows [!561](https://gitlab.com/orbit/team/orbit/-/merge_requests/561), which did the same for `resourceNames` and `nonResourceURLs`.\n\n**Upgrade note:** `helm install` and `helm upgrade` now fail if a rule sets a key other than `apiGroups`, `resources`, `verbs`, `resourceNames` or `nonResourceURLs`, or if a rule is not a map. The failure happens at render time. Nothing is applied, and the running Role stays as it is.\n\n- Fail when a rule sets an unsupported key, and list all such keys in one message.\n- Fail when a rule is not a map.\n- Keep the `resourceNames` and `nonResourceURLs` messages, and report them first.\n- Add 5 unit tests and update the `values.yaml` comment.\n\n## What's the best way to test this MR?\n\n```shell\nhelm unittest .\nhelm template r . --set gitlabUrl=https://gitlab.example.com --set runnerToken=dummy --set rbac.create=true --set \"rbac.rules[0].resources[0]=secrets\" --set \"rbac.rules[0].resource_names[0]=only-this-secret\" --show-only templates/role.yaml\n```\n\nThe render fails and names `rbac.rules[0]` and `resource_names`. On `main` it prints a rule with no names.\n\n## Related\n\nThe user docs for this setting are in https://gitlab.com/orbit/orbit/-/merge_requests/7629.",
